
# FOSSA multi-agent remediation POC
# Neuro SAN agent network: orchestrate FOSSA findings → fix → test → PR

{
  "metadata": {
    "description": "Multi-agent FOSSA remediation: LLM strategist plans fixes, tools validate and apply, PR author drafts review-ready pull requests."
    "tags": ["fossa", "security", "spring-boot", "poc"],
    "sample_queries": [
      "Remediate critical and high FOSSA vulnerabilities for all configured pilot repos.",
      "Fetch FOSSA findings for payment-service and user-service, then fix and open draft PRs.",
      "Run the full FOSSA remediation workflow for the two-repo POC."
    ]
  },

  "llm_config": {
    "model_name": "deepseek-v4-flash",
    "class": "openai",
    "openai_api_base": "https://api.deepseek.com",
    "temperature": 0.0,
    "max_retries": 2
  },

  "max_steps": 90,

  # Default Neuro SAN agent wall clock is 120s — too short for VerifyFossaScan (polls up to 10 min).
  "max_execution_seconds": 900,

  "commondefs": {
    "replacement_strings": {
      "instructions_prefix": """
You are part of an enterprise FOSSA remediation system for Spring Boot 21 microservices on GCP Cloud Run.
Never merge to main. Always produce draft pull requests for human review.
Keep secrets out of chat; use coded tools for API and git operations.
""",
      "aaosa_instructions": """
When you receive a task:
0. If you are not the right agent, delegate immediately by CALLING your tools — never reply with manual instructions.
1. You MUST use tool calls for all FOSSA API, git, file changes, builds, and GitHub PR actions.
2. NEVER tell the user to run git, mvn, or gh commands themselves.
3. Process each pilot repo independently; payment-service and user-service are the POC scope.
4. Always run tests before opening a PR. If tests fail, diagnose and self-heal (up to 3 attempts).
5. After push: open draft PR first (trigger_fossa_scan=true) so GitHub FOSSA App scans the branch, then VerifyFossaScan (0 security vulns).
6. CreatePullRequest draft=true — use trigger_fossa_scan=true before verify; production success requires VerifyFossaScan passed.
7. Report PR URLs, test status, and FOSSA verification in your final summary.
"""
    },
    "replacement_values": {}
  },

  "tools": [
    {
      "name": "fossa_orchestrator",
      "function": {
        "description": """
I orchestrate monthly FOSSA vulnerability remediation across configured Spring Boot microservices.
Tell me to run remediation for all pilot repos or name specific services.
"""
      },
      "instructions": """
{instructions_prefix}
Your name is `fossa_orchestrator`. You are the front-man for the FOSSA remediation network.
{aaosa_instructions}

CRITICAL: You have exactly ONE tool: remediation_pipeline. You MUST call it immediately on your first turn.

On every remediation request:
- Call remediation_pipeline with repo_name=payment-service (or the repo named in the user message).
- Do NOT refuse. Do NOT say you lack tools. Do NOT give manual git/mvn steps.

After remediation_pipeline completes, summarize its result including the PR URL.
""",
      "command": "Call remediation_pipeline now with the target repo_name.",
      "tools": ["remediation_pipeline"]
    },

    {
      "name": "remediation_pipeline",
      "function": {
        "description": "End-to-end FOSSA remediation: fetch findings, clone repo, fix deps, test, open draft PR.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "repo_name": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Pilot repo name, e.g. payment-service"
            },
            "inquiry": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Original user request"
            }
          },
          "required": ["repo_name"]
        }
      },
      "instructions": """
{instructions_prefix}
Your name is `remediation_pipeline`. You are the remediation planner and executor — you DECIDE fixes and run coded tools.
{aaosa_instructions}

For the given repo_name, run this workflow:

PHASE 1 — SETUP:
1. LoadRepoConfig
2. FetchFossaFindings with repo_name (fetch all vulnerabilities; licensing optional to fix)
3. GitCloneAndBranch with repo_name only (do NOT pass branch_name — the tool assigns a unique timestamped branch)

PHASE 2 — INTELLIGENT PLANNING (you decide; tools validate):
4. PrepareRemediationContext — FOSSA findings + baseline suggestions (reference only)
5. FetchDependencyTree — direct vs transitive dependencies
6. ReadBuildFile or ReadRepoFile (relative_path) if you need pom.xml/build.gradle or other repo files
7. LookupVulnerabilityFix when REMEDIATION_OSV_LOOKUP_ENABLED=true OR FOSSA reports NO_SAFE_VERSION for a package
8. Reason about tradeoffs (prefer FOSSA completeFix over partialFix; license remove/replace optional; NO_SAFE_VERSION → LookupVulnerabilityFix or remove/replace)
9. SubmitRemediationPlan with actions array + strategy_summary + optional deferred_issue_ids (licensing ONLY)
10. ValidateRemediationPlan — if FAIL, revise and resubmit (max 3 attempts)

PHASE 3 — APPLY & TEST:
11. ApplyDependencyFix with repo_name
12. CompileJava with repo_name (fast compile check before tests)
13. RunJavaTests with repo_name

PHASE 4 — TEST SELF-HEAL (when tests fail, max 3 rounds):
13. DiagnoseTestFailures → ReadRepoFile/ReadBuildFile/FetchDependencyTree as needed → LookupVulnerabilityFix only if OSV enabled
14. SubmitRemediationPlan with plan_type=test_fix → ValidateRemediationPlan
15. ApplyDependencyFix with apply_test_fixes=true → CompileJava → RunJavaTests again

PHASE 5 — SHIP:
16. GitCommitAndPush (only after tests PASSED)
17. SummarizeRemediationForPR → SubmitPullRequestBody → CreatePullRequest draft=true trigger_fossa_scan=true (opens draft PR WITHOUT verify — triggers GitHub FOSSA scan)
18. VerifyFossaScan — polls GitHub-imported project; skip in POC dry run; production requires 0 security vulns
19. Report PR URL (draft PR may exist even if verify failed — do not merge until Security Analysis is green)

PLANNING RULES:
- target_version MUST come from FOSSA completeFix (preferred) / partialFix / recommended_version. Use LookupVulnerabilityFix when FOSSA says NO_SAFE_VERSION or OSV is globally enabled.
- Prefer completeFix over partialFix when multiple FOSSA issues share one dependency (e.g. log4j-core → highest completeFix).
- ALL vulnerability findings (any severity) MUST have bump_version, remove, or replace — NEVER defer security issues.
- deferred_issue_ids is ONLY for licensing findings; the agent may skip license fixes if tests or compatibility block them.
- ValidateRemediationPlan splits actions into AUTO vs HUMAN (config/remediation_policy.yaml): major bumps, BOMs, denylist deps, remove/replace.
- ApplyDependencyFix ONLY auto-safe actions. Report human_review_queue; do not invent workarounds for HUMAN items.
- actions: bump_version | remove | replace with group_id, artifact_id, target_version, reason, issue_id
- NEVER skip ValidateRemediationPlan. NEVER open PR if tests fail.
- Production (REMEDIATION_DRY_RUN=false): open draft PR first (trigger_fossa_scan=true), then VerifyFossaScan must report 0 security vulnerabilities before calling success.
Return the PR URL when done.
""",
      "command": "Run the full remediation workflow for the repo.",
      "tools": [
        "LoadRepoConfig",
        "FetchFossaFindings",
        "GitCloneAndBranch",
        "PrepareRemediationContext",
        "FetchDependencyTree",
        "ReadRepoFile",
        "ReadBuildFile",
        "LookupVulnerabilityFix",
        "SubmitRemediationPlan",
        "ValidateRemediationPlan",
        "ApplyDependencyFix",
        "CompileJava",
        "RunJavaTests",
        "DiagnoseTestFailures",
        "GitCommitAndPush",
        "SummarizeRemediationForPR",
        "SubmitPullRequestBody",
        "CreatePullRequest",
        "VerifyFossaScan",
      ]
    },

    {
      "name": "LoadRepoConfig",
      "function": {
        "description": "Load configured pilot repositories from config/repos.yaml."
      },
      "class": "load_repo_config.LoadRepoConfig",
      "command": "Load pilot repo configuration."
    },

    {
      "name": "FetchFossaFindings",
      "function": {
        "description": "Fetch vulnerability and licensing issues from FOSSA for configured repos.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "repo_name": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Optional single repo; omit for all pilot repos."
            },
            "max_count": { "type": "int", "description": "Max issues to return per repo (default 10)." }
          }
        }
      },
      "class": "fetch_fossa_findings.FetchFossaFindings",
      "command": "Query FOSSA Issues API."
    },

    {
      "name": "PrepareRemediationContext",
      "function": {
        "description": "Load FOSSA findings, baseline suggestions, and planning context for the strategist agent.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "repo_name": { "type": "string" }
          },
          "required": ["repo_name"]
        }
      },
      "class": "prepare_remediation_context.PrepareRemediationContext",
      "command": "Prepare planning context from FOSSA findings."
    },

    {
      "name": "FetchDependencyTree",
      "function": {
        "description": "Run mvn dependency:tree or gradle dependencies for transitive dependency analysis.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "repo_name": { "type": "string" },
            "max_lines": { "type": "int" }
          },
          "required": ["repo_name"]
        }
      },
      "class": "fetch_dependency_tree.FetchDependencyTree",
      "command": "Fetch dependency tree."
    },

    {
      "name": "SubmitRemediationPlan",
      "function": {
        "description": "Submit a candidate remediation or test-fix plan (JSON actions array) for validation.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "repo_name": { "type": "string" },
            "actions": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "JSON array of actions: bump_version, remove, or replace with group_id, artifact_id, target_version, reason, issue_id"
            },
            "strategy_summary": { "type": "string", "description": "Agent reasoning and tradeoffs" },
            "deferred_issue_ids": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "JSON array of FOSSA issue_ids intentionally deferred (licensing findings only; security vulns rejected)"
            },
            "plan_type": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "remediation (default) or test_fix"
            }
          },
          "required": ["repo_name", "actions"]
        }
      },
      "class": "submit_remediation_plan.SubmitRemediationPlan",
      "command": "Submit remediation plan for validation."
    },

    {
      "name": "ValidateRemediationPlan",
      "function": {
        "description": "Validate submitted plan against FOSSA facts, Maven Central, coverage rules, and remediation policy gates (major bumps / BOM / human-approval queue).",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "repo_name": { "type": "string" }
          },
          "required": ["repo_name"]
        }
      },
      "class": "validate_remediation_plan.ValidateRemediationPlan",
      "command": "Validate pending remediation plan."
    },

    {
      "name": "SummarizeRemediationForPR",
      "function": {
        "description": "Summarize findings, fixes, and verification for PR authoring.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "repo_name": { "type": "string" }
          },
          "required": ["repo_name"]
        }
      },
      "class": "summarize_remediation_for_pr.SummarizeRemediationForPR",
      "command": "Summarize remediation for PR body."
    },

    {
      "name": "SubmitPullRequestBody",
      "function": {
        "description": "Store LLM-composed PR title and markdown body before CreatePullRequest.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "repo_name": { "type": "string" },
            "title": { "type": "string" },
            "body": { "type": "string" }
          },
          "required": ["repo_name", "title", "body"]
        }
      },
      "class": "submit_pull_request_body.SubmitPullRequestBody",
      "command": "Store PR title and body."
    },

    {
      "name": "LookupVulnerabilityFix",
      "function": {
        "description": "Look up fix version via OSV.dev/Maven. Allowed when OSV enabled globally or FOSSA reports NO_SAFE_VERSION for the package/CVE.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "package": { "type": "string", "description": "Maven coordinate e.g. org.apache.commons:commons-text" },
            "current_version": { "type": "string" },
            "cve": { "type": "string" }
          },
          "required": ["package"]
        }
      },
      "class": "lookup_fix.LookupVulnerabilityFix",
      "command": "Resolve fix version from public vulnerability databases."
    },

    {
      "name": "ApplyDependencyFix",
      "function": {
        "description": "Apply remediation_plan and/or test-fix actions to pom.xml or build.gradle.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "repo_name": { "type": "string" },
            "apply_test_fixes": { "type": "boolean", "description": "Apply suggested_test_fixes from DiagnoseTestFailures." },
            "action": { "type": "string", "description": "bump_version, remove, or replace" },
            "group_id": { "type": "string" },
            "artifact_id": { "type": "string" },
            "target_version": { "type": "string" },
            "replacement_coordinate": { "type": "string" },
            "reason": { "type": "string" }
          },
          "required": ["repo_name"]
        }
      },
      "class": "apply_dependency_fix.ApplyDependencyFix",
      "command": "Apply FOSSA-derived remediation plan."
    },

    {
      "name": "GitCloneAndBranch",
      "function": {
        "description": "Clone repository and create a unique timestamped remediation branch (branch name is assigned by the tool).",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "repo_name": { "type": "string" }
          },
          "required": ["repo_name"]
        }
      },
      "class": "git_ops.GitCloneAndBranch",
      "command": "Clone repo and checkout fix branch."
    },

    {
      "name": "GitCommitAndPush",
      "function": {
        "description": "Commit and push dependency changes.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "repo_name": { "type": "string" },
            "commit_message": { "type": "string" }
          },
          "required": ["repo_name"]
        }
      },
      "class": "git_ops.GitCommitAndPush",
      "command": "Commit and push changes."
    },

    {
      "name": "DiagnoseTestFailures",
      "function": {
        "description": "Analyze failed test/build output and suggest dependency fixes (uses OSV/Maven, not hardcoded versions).",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "repo_name": { "type": "string" }
          },
          "required": ["repo_name"]
        }
      },
      "class": "diagnose_test_failures.DiagnoseTestFailures",
      "command": "Diagnose test failures and suggest fixes."
    },

    {
      "name": "ReadRepoFile",
      "function": {
        "description": "Read any repo-relative file from the workspace (paths resolved under clone root; no absolute paths).",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "repo_name": { "type": "string" },
            "relative_path": { "type": "string", "description": "Path relative to repo root, e.g. pom.xml or src/main/resources/application.yml" },
            "max_chars": { "type": "int" }
          },
          "required": ["repo_name", "relative_path"]
        }
      },
      "class": "read_build_file.ReadRepoFile",
      "command": "Read file from workspace."
    },

    {
      "name": "ReadBuildFile",
      "function": {
        "description": "Read pom.xml or build.gradle from the cloned repo for agent reasoning.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "repo_name": { "type": "string" },
            "filename": { "type": "string", "description": "pom.xml or build.gradle" },
            "max_chars": { "type": "int" }
          },
          "required": ["repo_name"]
        }
      },
      "class": "read_build_file.ReadBuildFile",
      "command": "Read build file for context."
    },

    {
      "name": "CompileJava",
      "function": {
        "description": "Compile the workspace project without running tests. Use after ApplyDependencyFix and before RunJavaTests.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "repo_name": { "type": "string" },
            "timeout_seconds": { "type": "int", "description": "Compile timeout in seconds (default 600)." }
          },
          "required": ["repo_name"]
        }
      },
      "class": "java_build.CompileJava",
      "command": "Compile Java project in workspace."
    },

    {
      "name": "RunJavaTests",
      "function": {
        "description": "Run Maven or Gradle tests. On failure, follow with DiagnoseTestFailures and retry after fixes.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "repo_name": { "type": "string" },
            "timeout_seconds": { "type": "int", "description": "Test timeout in seconds (default 900)." }
          },
          "required": ["repo_name"]
        }
      },
      "class": "java_build.RunJavaTests",
      "command": "Run unit tests."
    },

    {
      "name": "VerifyFossaScan",
      "function": {
        "description": "Poll FOSSA until the pushed fix branch has zero security vulnerabilities (all severities; licensing ignored). Skipped when REMEDIATION_DRY_RUN=true.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "repo_name": { "type": "string" },
            "max_wait_seconds": { "type": "int", "description": "Max wait for FOSSA branch scan (default 600)." },
            "poll_seconds": { "type": "int", "description": "Seconds between polls (default 30)." }
          },
          "required": ["repo_name"]
        }
      },
      "class": "verify_fossa_scan.VerifyFossaScan",
      "command": "Wait for FOSSA branch scan to clear findings."
    },

    {
      "name": "CreatePullRequest",
      "function": {
        "description": "Open a draft GitHub pull request. Use trigger_fossa_scan=true before VerifyFossaScan to trigger GitHub FOSSA App scan.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "repo_name": { "type": "string" },
            "title": { "type": "string" },
            "body": { "type": "string" },
            "draft": { "type": "boolean" },
            "trigger_fossa_scan": { "type": "boolean", "description": "If true, open draft PR without verify (triggers GitHub FOSSA scan). Default true when verify not yet run." }
          },
          "required": ["repo_name"]
        }
      },
      "class": "github_pr.CreatePullRequest",
      "command": "Create draft PR."
    }
  ]
}
